[medium] If even one resource fails to fetch (e.g., offline at install time, a 404, or an opaque response), `cache.addAll(APP_RESOURCES)` rejects as a whole, which can block the SW from installing or updating. Worth wrapping in try/catch and/or caching items individually with `Promise.allSettled`, and deciding up front whether install should fail hard or continue with a partial cache.

```suggestion
async function addFilesToCache() {
  const cache = await caches.open(CACHE);
  const results = await Promise.allSettled(APP_RESOURCES.map((p) => cache.add(p)));
  // Optionally: if you want to fail install on critical assets, detect rejections here
  const failed = results.filter((r) => r.status === 'rejected');
  if (failed.length) {
    // log or decide whether to throw
  }
}
```
